;
; F16 join-multiplicity witness (session-27, the P6.3 A1 close). The recursive
; producer of `r` join-binds BOTH head ordinals from TWO distinct in-cycle
; sources: head r.A is fed by r.A (identity, from `r(A,C)`) AND by r.B (non-
; identity, from `r(B,A)`); symmetrically for r.B. Its routes are
;   r.A->r.A, r.B->r.B, r.A->r.B, r.B->r.A
; so the value at each head ordinal is determined by a JOIN of two recursive
; rows, NOT a clean identity carry. The correct fusion classification is
; therefore JOINT.
;
; This is the DISCRIMINATOR for the F16 single-source guard in
; `ClassifyFusableComponents` (Planning.cpp): the pre-guard (F16-LAX) code saw
; only the identity route on each ordinal and WRONGLY emitted
;   fused-fixpoint  C0  binding-prefix=(A, B)
; the F16-CLOSED code sees the >=2 distinct in-cycle sources per ordinal and
; correctly emits `joint-fixpoint  C0` (mirroring PromoteSharedSymbolicField's
; single-source promotion rule). The `.region` golden's joint-fixpoint block is
; the gate; answers are recursion-classification-invariant (the M3 backend
; materializes `r` identically in every mode). A genuinely additive triangle
; recursion (NOT a vacuous self-reference) so the multi-view SCC survives
; canonicalization in all four optimization modes.
#message edge_2(u64 A, u64 B).
#message out_pair(u64 A, u64 B).

#local r(u64 A, u64 B).

r(A, B) : edge_2(A, B).
r(A, B) : r(A, C), r(C, B), r(B, A).

out_pair(A, B) : r(A, B).
